1|0@leagueoflegends^1440580552#cug2xoc:Wafflashizzles$:Holy shit, you're fucking special. They've literally said it themselves, and explained it in detail, but because you're too much of a special snowflake to do it yourself, please, allow me to explain. When you move the datacenter for one of the largest games in NA from California to Illinois, you are moving incredible amounts of traffic and data to a new location from the old. Imagine data from an LoL game is like a refrigerator truck on a freeway. It's carrying perishables. The faster that truck goes from the factory (datacenter) to the supermarket (your house), the fresher the produce is- or in this case, the better the ping. If the freeway is clear, your shit gets to the market real quick, and you're good to go. Unfortunately, this freeway is in the middle of fucking boston, and it's rush hour right now, so your truck is shit out of luck. In essence, this is what happens to your data on LoL when riot isn't partnered with an ISP- your data gets crowded out and slowed down by the rest. it's unavoidable. However, when riot partners with an ISP, it's the same as reserving a lane ONLY for all the food trucks from that one particular factory. You bypass all the other traffic because you don't need to travel through the same lanes. The reason why so many people have uber shit ping right now on the west coast is because riot is still in talks to partner with several major ISPS at their new datacenter- two of those they are still talking to are AT&amp;T and Verizon. But you're probably too fucking frothy to even bother reading what i've just said. So rage away. Quit if you want bru, the world won't weep for your loss. I promise.
